          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            Recall (eg. from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "monad#RelationBetweenAdjunctionsAndMonads"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint+functor"} right adjoint functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\dashv G \,\colon\, \mathcal{B}\to\mathcal{A}
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\circ F
          %p
            The notion of the
            %em codensity monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^G
            is a generalization of this construction to functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \colon \mathcal{B}\to\mathcal{A}
            that need not be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints"} right adjoints
            but do at least admit a right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi G
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ran_G G
            along themselves, such that both constructions agree when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is in fact a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
          %p
            The name ‘codensity monad’ stems from the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^G
            reduces to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity
            monad iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \colon \mathcal{B}\to\mathcal{A}
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codense+functor"} codense functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to be codense”.
          %p
            The same idea applies to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
            more general than
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #codensity_monad.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (codensity monad)
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \colon \mathcal{B}\to\mathcal{A}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              whose
              %a{:href => "Kan+extension#Pointwise"} pointwise
              right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ran
                      %mi G
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≡
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi T
