            %p
              and finally finish the proof by observing that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ε
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon
              coequalizes
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi μ
                        %mi G
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^G G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mi G
                      %mi ε
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^G \varepsilon
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Every monad that is
              %a{:href => "monad#RelationBetweenAdjunctionsAndMonads"} induced
              by an adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
              is the codensity monad of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+monad"} enriched monad
              is a codensity monad (via its
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              be an object in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d : 1 \to C
              is the
              %strong double dualization monad
              associated to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^{d^{(-)}}
            %p
              More conceptually, the codensity monad construction may be seen as a generalisation of the double dualisation construction analogous to the generalisation from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+for+a+monad"} algebras for a monad
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules+over+a+monad"} modules over a monad
              (the latter is the perspective that is most natural 2-categorically).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
              (as well as a finitely additive version) arise as codensity monads of forgetful functors from subcategories of the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+sets"} convex sets
              to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+spaces"} measurable spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "#Avery14"}> Avery 14
              ).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The codensity monad of the inclusion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter"} ultrafilter
              monad. Its algebras are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The codensity monad of the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FinGrp
                    %mo ↪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinGrp \hookrightarrow
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+completion+of+a+group"} profinite completion
              monad, whose algebras may be identified with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+groups"} profinite groups
              – that is,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
              whose underlying topological space is profinite (
              %a{:href => "#Avery17"}> Avery 17, Proposition 2.7.10
              ).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The codensity monad of the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet \to Top
              computes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+spectrum"} Stone spectrum
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clopen+subsets"} clopen subsets
              of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+spaces"} Stone spaces
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Sipos"} Sipoș, Theorem 2
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The codensity monad of the inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo →
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \to Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              consisting of arbitrary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+products"} small products
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+space"} Sierpiński space
              %span.newWikiWord
                localic spectrum
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/localic+spectrum"} ?
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
              of opens of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+spaces"} sober spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Sipos"} Sipoș, Theorem 6
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The codensity monad of the inclusion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+sets"} countable sets
              in all sets,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ctbl
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ctbl \hookrightarrow Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the set of ultrafilters on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              closed under countable intersections. This still holds for the inclusion of the full subcategory of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ctbl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ctbl
              on the single set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              More generally, the codensity monad of the inclusion of sets of cardinality less than that of fixed
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi Y
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_{\lt Y} \hookrightarrow Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the set of
              = succeed "-complete" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              For the codensity monad induced by the inclusion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types+with+finite+homotopy+groups"} homotopy types with finite homotopy groups
              into all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "homotopy+type+with+finite+homotopy+groups#CodensityMonadOfInclusionIntoAllHomotopyTypes"} there
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The codensity monad induced by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              is isomorphic to the monad induced by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+adjunction"} Isbell adjunction
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              In the bicategory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"} Rel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T: A \to C
              along a relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: A \to B
              is the relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/R: B \to C
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b,c)\in T/R
              iff
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{a: A}\; R(a, b) \Rightarrow T(a, c)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/R
              reduces to the identity relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_B
              iff whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b,b')
              is such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{a:A}\; R(a,b)\Rightarrow R(a,b')
              then
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b=b'\,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^{-1}b\subseteq R^{-1}b'
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b=b'
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/R: B \to B
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rel
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/specialization+order"} specialization order
              for a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
            %p
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : B \to A
              be a functor admitting a codensity monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^G
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^G
              has homs
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Kl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Kl(T^G)(a, a') \cong [B, Set](B(a', G-), B(a, G-))
          %p
            See
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BC80"} Bourn and Cordier 1980
